The `NullReferenceException` in `Enemy.PerformAttack()` at line 383, specifically `_player.GlobalPosition`, occurs because `_player` is `null` when a ranged enemy attempts to fire a projectile. Although `ProcessChasing` correctly uses `previousPlayerPosition` if `_player` is `null` for movement, `PerformAttack` does not.

To resolve this, I will modify `PerformAttack()` to use `previousPlayerPosition` as the target if `_player` is `null`.

**Proposed Fix:**

```csharp
	private void PerformAttack()
	{
		AudioManager.Play(AudioPlayer_Attack, (AudioFile)AudioData["Attack"]);
